senses.gloss:
लिख् (cf. the earlier form √ रिख्) cl. 6. P. (Dhātup. xxviii, 72) लिख॑ति (rarely Ā. ˚ते; pf. लिले॑ख, Br. &c.; aor. अलेखीत्, ib.; fut. लेखिता, लेखिष्यति Gr.; लिखिष्यति, Hariv.; inf. लेखितुम्, or लिखितुम् Gr.; ind.p. लेखित्वा, ib.; लिखित्वा, Hariv.; -लि॑ख्य, Br. &c.),
to scratch, scrape, furrow, tear up (the ground), AV. &c. &c.;
to pick, peck (said of birds), VarBṛS.; Hit.;
to scarify, lance, Suśr.;
to produce by scratching &c., draw a line (with or scil. लेखाम्), engrave, inscribe, write, copy, trace, sketch, delineate, paint, Br. &c. &c.;
to make smooth, polish, MārkP.;
to graze, touch, MW.;
to unite sexually with a female (?), MBh. xiii, 2456 (Nīlak.) :
Pass. लिख्यते (aor. अलेखि), to be written, Kathās.; Pañcat. :
Caus. लेखयति (or लिखापयति; aor. अलीलिखत्),
to cause to scratch or write or copy or paint, ŚāṅkhŚr.; Mn. &c.;
to scratch, lance, Suśr.;
to write, paint, Yājñ. :
Desid. लिलिखिषति or लिलेखिषति, Pāṇ. i, 2, 26.
